@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@
     Do not mistake a loud, confrontational tone for a strong question. Nepali AGMs, like most formal gatherings, are chaired by a person with authority to limit or close off disorderly conduct. A shareholder who shouts often gets removed from the discussion procedurally, while a shareholder who asks a sharp, calm, specific question is far harder to dismiss and far more likely to get a complete answer recorded in the minutes.
