   <p>Nepal's primary market operates under a specific legal and institutional framework that every serious investor should understand. The Securities Act, 2063 (2006) is the foundational legislation. SEBON — the Securities Board of Nepal — is the apex regulatory authority, equivalent to the SEC in the United States or SEBI in India. NEPSE — the Nepal Stock Exchange — is the trading venue where approved securities are listed and subsequently traded.</p>
