   <p>The rights ratio expresses the entitlement offered to existing shareholders. A 1:5 rights issue, for example, means that for every five shares currently held, the shareholder is entitled to subscribe to one new share. A 1:1 rights issue — sometimes called a 'one-for-one' or a 100% rights issue — means the company is doubling its share count, with each existing shareholder entitled to one new share for each they already hold.</p>
