   <p>The most significant barrier facing a new investor in Nepal is not lack of capital — it is lack of knowledge architecture. Investing in individual stocks requires understanding financial statements, sectoral dynamics, management quality, valuation methodologies, market microstructure, and portfolio construction. For someone starting from zero, the learning curve is steep and the potential for costly mistakes during the learning period is high.</p>
