+  <h2 id="lesson-28-6-a-practical-red-flag-checklist-for-the-nepali">Lesson 28.6 — A Practical Red-Flag Checklist for the Nepali Investor</h2>
   <p>Everything in this chapter converges on a discipline you can actually run, counter by counter, before committing capital. No single item on the checklist below is sufficient grounds to avoid a stock outright, and conversely, a company that clears every item is not guaranteed to be clean — red-flag analysis raises or lowers your probability estimate and your required margin of safety, it does not replace fundamental valuation. But an investor who mechanically works through a checklist like this one, for every NEPSE-listed BFI or non-bank company under serious consideration, will catch a meaningful share of the problems this chapter has described before those problems surface in a price collapse or a regulatory action.</p>
