   <p>If inventory is the largest asset, the working capital cycle is the clock that tells you how efficiently a company turns that asset into cash. This is the single most useful analytical lens for distinguishing manufacturing businesses from trading businesses in Nepal, because their cycles run at genuinely different speeds and for different structural reasons.</p>
   <p>The cash conversion cycle (CCC) is built from three components, each measured in days:</p>
