     In Nepal, a capital loss on listed shares is a documented claim you build and may need to defend, not a number your broker automatically nets against a gain elsewhere in your portfolio. Plan your loss realisation around the fiscal year-end (Ashad) as a deliberate annual review, keep every contract note, and treat any offset claim as work for a qualified tax preparer — not a checkbox in your trading app.
