   <p>Asset quality, capital, and solvency ratios tell you whether a company can survive stress. Efficiency ratios tell you how well it converts its resources — staff, branches, or fixed assets — into revenue during normal times. They are the ratios that separate a well-run company from a merely solvent one.</p>
