   <p>A hydropower financial model is, at its core, a very long spreadsheet that tries to answer one question: will the water flowing down a Himalayan river generate enough cash, over enough years, to repay the people who financed the dam, turbine, and powerhouse — and still leave something for the equity owners? Everything else in this chapter is detail layered onto that single question.</p>
