   <p>Every insurer in Nepal is regulated not by Nepal Rastra Bank (NRB), which oversees banks and development banks, but by a separate authority — the Nepal Insurance Authority, known until a 2022 rebranding as Beema Samiti (beema is the Nepali word for insurance). This is a distinction worth fixing firmly in your head as a NEPSE investor, because it is easy to assume every financial company answers to the central bank. It does not. NRB sets the rules for deposit-taking institutions; the Nepal Insurance Authority sets the rules for insurers and reinsurers, and its rulebook is built around a different central question than NRB's: not "can this institution meet withdrawal requests," but "does this insurer hold enough capital, over and above its reserves, to withstand claims coming in worse than expected?"</p>
